WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.874
Deep work needs a box.

00:00:01.874 --> 00:00:03.373
Open-ended evenings become scrolling.

00:00:03.373 --> 00:00:05.997
This lesson is about time boxing practice.

00:00:05.997 --> 00:00:07.121
45-minute deep blocks.

00:00:07.121 --> 00:00:09.745
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:09.745 --> 00:00:13.493
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:19.115
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.115 --> 00:00:23.237
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:27.360
Stay practical: schedule two blocks before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.581
Use forty-five minute deep blocks.

00:00:29.581 --> 00:00:30.341
Phone away.

00:00:30.341 --> 00:00:31.861
One outcome per block.

00:00:31.861 --> 00:00:34.142
Remember the objective: schedule two blocks.

00:00:34.142 --> 00:00:38.323
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:38.323 --> 00:00:42.884
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:47.066
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.066 --> 00:00:51.627
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:51.627 --> 00:00:54.288
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:54.288 --> 00:00:55.808
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:56.128 --> 00:00:59.381
Schedule two blocks this week on a real calendar.

00:00:59.381 --> 00:01:02.272
Protect them like a meeting with a customer.

00:01:02.272 --> 00:01:04.440
Remember the objective: schedule two blocks.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.415
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:08.415 --> 00:01:12.752
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:12.752 --> 00:01:16.727
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:01:16.727 --> 00:01:21.064
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:01:21.384 --> 00:01:23.248
When the box ends, stop.

00:01:23.248 --> 00:01:24.739
Note the next action.

00:01:24.739 --> 00:01:27.348
That is how consistency beats hero days.

00:01:27.348 --> 00:01:29.585
Remember the objective: schedule two blocks.

00:01:29.585 --> 00:01:33.685
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:01:33.685 --> 00:01:38.158
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:01:38.158 --> 00:01:42.259
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:46.732
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:01:46.732 --> 00:01:49.341
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:50.832
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:54.338
